  <h1>Guides</h1>

  <p>In-depth, plain-language guides covering the major topics in elder abuse and nursing home neglect claims. Each is written and reviewed by our editorial team and includes citations to primary sources &mdash; state Elder Abuse Acts, OBRA regulations, CMS F-Tag definitions, and the leading appellate decisions on heightened damages.</p>

  <h2>The four core guides</h2>

  <h3><a href="/guides/how-elder-abuse-settlements-are-calculated">How Elder Abuse Settlements Are Calculated</a></h3>
  <p>A detailed walkthrough of the damages categories, the role of state Elder Abuse Acts (especially California &sect; 15657 enhanced remedies), the F-Tag evidence framework, wrongful death overlays, and worked examples covering pressure ulcers, financial exploitation, and wrongful death from neglect.</p>

  <h3><a href="/guides/recognizing-elder-abuse-and-nursing-home-neglect">Recognizing Elder Abuse and Nursing Home Neglect</a></h3>
  <p>The warning signs across the seven recognized abuse categories, how to interpret CMS survey reports and F-Tag deficiencies, the role of Adult Protective Services, and what an APS investigation actually does.</p>

  <h3><a href="/guides/what-to-do-if-you-suspect-elder-abuse">What to Do If You Suspect Elder Abuse</a></h3>
  <p>Step-by-step practical guidance: APS reporting, evidence preservation, attorney consultation, family communication, facility-management escalation, and the timing decisions that materially affect both the elder&rsquo;s safety and any later civil claim.</p>

  <h3><a href="/guides/common-elder-abuse-claim-misconceptions">Common Elder Abuse Claim Misconceptions</a></h3>
  <p>Fifteen common misunderstandings about elder abuse compensation &mdash; from APS reporting consequences to F-Tag evidence to the under-appreciated importance of analyzing pre-dispute arbitration clauses in nursing home admission contracts &mdash; with the actual rules and practical implications.</p>

